I'd like to talk about a time when my best friend persuaded me to do something important, and in the end, I was really glad that I listened to him.
It happened about give years ago when I was in my second year at university. At that time, I was in a relationship that had already lasted for more than a year. Although we had some good moments together, the relationship gradually became quite unhealthy. My girlfriend was often cold and distant, and whenever we argued, I usually felt like everything was my fault. Because of that, I became emotionally exhausted and stressed most of the time.

Since my best friend and I were very close, I often talked to him about my relationship problems. One day, after listening to me complain for hours, he seriously advised me to break up with her. He told me that he had noticed a big change in my personality and that I seemed much more negative and unhappy than before. He also said that I deserved to be with someone who truly cared about me and respected me.

At first, I didn’t want to accept his advice because I still had feelings for her. However, after thinking carefully about everything for about a week, I realized he was right. Eventually, I decided to end the relationship.

Honestly, it was one of the hardest decisions I had ever made. For a while, I felt really depressed and even considered getting back together with her. Fortunately, my best friend stayed by my side the whole time. He kept encouraging me, cheering me up, and reminding me why I had made that decision in the first place.

Looking back now, I’m genuinely happy that he persuaded me to do it because my mental health improved a lot afterward. I became more confident, more positive, and more focused on myself. I also learned that sometimes people outside a relationship can see things more clearly than the people involved in it.
